diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1342a73
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+Feature: Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to navigate between filter views using the URL and browser history
+  So I can use the back button to return to a previous view
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Filter link updates the URL hash
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    When I click the "Active" filter
+    Then the URL hash should be "#/active"
+
+  Scenario: Hashchange re-renders the todo list
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    And I have a completed todo "Buy eggs"
+    When I navigate to "#/active"
+    Then I should see "Buy milk" in the todo list
+    And I should not see "Buy eggs" in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Back button returns to previous filter view
+    Given I have a todo "Buy milk"
+    And I have a completed todo "Buy eggs"
+    When I click the "Active" filter
+    Then I should see "Buy milk" in the todo list
+    And I should not see "Buy eggs" in the todo list
+    When I navigate back
+    Then I should see "Buy milk" in the todo list
+    And I should see "Buy eggs" in the todo list
+
+  Scenario: Filter handler must not prevent anchor default navigation
+    Given the app source at "js/app.js"
+    Then the filter click handler does not call "preventDefault"
